~ intro
Melos: The world has lost its colors and its melody... Everything is frozen in a grey, heavy silence.
Melos: I must restore harmony. By solving these puzzles, I will bring life and vibrance back to this world!
Game: Welcome, Melos. This is your first trial. To restore harmony, you must prove your worth by mastering the laws of sound. Only then will the Spirits of Music agree to help you.
Game: Good luck on your journey!
=> END

~ start
Melos: This door... it seems to react to my presence. There is no lock; I should try to interact with it to see if it opens.
=> END

~ hint
Melos: It is waiting for an answer. I must mimic that echo. These strings on the ground... if I interact with them, I can make them vibrate!
Harmony Guide: [HINT] String length determines pitch. Long strings are heavy and slow, creating a Deep sound. Short strings are light and fast, creating a High sound.
=> END

~ lesson
Melos: A page... it detached itself from the door's structure.
Harmony Guide: [GRIMOIRE UPDATED]
Harmony Guide: LESSON I: THE DIMENSION OF SOUND. Length dictates the note.
Harmony Guide: Long String = Low Frequency. Large objects vibrate slower, creating a Deep sound.
Harmony Guide: Short String = High Frequency. Small objects vibrate faster, creating a High sound.
=> END